            <ArticleTitle>Tc-99m tetrofosmin reverse perfusion pattern with ST segment depression after dipyridamole infusion in a patient with unstable angina and no evident coronary artery stenoses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>131-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Reverse redistribution is a well-known pattern found when performing thallium myocardial scintigraphy, and it has been implicated as an indicator of myocardial ischemia. Much more rarely, when using technetium compounds, which do not redistribute, a similar pattern is noted after the second injection of the radiotracer. This pattern has been termed &quot;reverse perfusion pattern,&quot; and its full implications are not yet clear and are still being investigated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
